Error [jet.StringViewOutlivesOwner]: `result` cannot be returned without an owning copy
  --> tests/ui/ownership/returned_string_view_cannot_outlive_local_owner.jet:4:12
    |
  4 |     return result
    |            ^^^^^^
 Why: `result` is a zero-copy view into `email` (`.trim()`/`.after()`/`.before()`); this destination needs an owned `String`, and `copies: .Explicit` keeps the implicit materialization disabled
 Fix: Write `result.copy()` first, or remove `copies: .Explicit` to use the default owning copy
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2307
